From 592c8be6278292408df5c532b2d0736fd67d19ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George J Padayatti <george.padayatti@igrant.io>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 01:54:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] INTEGRATION.md: fresh-installation guide for the
 iGrant.io package and the learner journey

---
 examples/INTEGRATION.md | 141 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 141 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 examples/INTEGRATION.md

diff --git a/examples/INTEGRATION.md b/examples/INTEGRATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..473f9f47
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/INTEGRATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,141 @@
+# iGrant.io on a fresh Liquio installation
+
+How to go from a clean Liquio deployment to the three learner-journey services
+in the cabinet: **Register as a learner**, **Educational certificate**, and
+**Apply for a job**.
+
+## What the package contains
+
+One patch (or the `feature/igrantio-credential-component` branch) with:
+
+| Part | Path | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Event plugin | `packages/event-igrantio-plugin` | Issue / verify / checkStatus / revoke / supplyClaims against OWS from BPMN event nodes |
+| Reader plugin | `packages/external-reader-igrantio-plugin` | Exchange-status polling for the cabinet form |
+| Form control | `packages/front-core/components/JsonSchema/elements/IgrantCredential` + registration in `components/cabinet-front` | The wallet QR panel (`igrant.credential`) |
+| Config templates | `config-templates/event/*`, `config-templates/external-reader/*` | plugins.json / services.json / requester.json examples |
+| Helm blocks | `helm-chart/templates/core-services/event.configmap.yaml`, `external-reader.configmap.yaml` | Same wiring for Kubernetes |
+| Settings register | `examples/register-200-200.dat` | The register that holds the OWS base URL + API key |
+| Workflows | `examples/workflow-1004-register-learner.bpmn`, `examples/workflow-1003-educational-certificate.bpmn`, `examples/workflow-1005-apply-for-a-job.bpmn` | The three services |
+
+## Step 1 — Apply the code and build
+
+1. Apply `igrantio-credential-component.patch` on the Liquio source
+   (`git am igrantio-credential-component.patch`).
+2. Build the two plugins (`npm install && npm run build && npm pack` in each
+   package), or publish them to your npm registry. The pack step produces
+   `liquio-event-igrantio-plugin-<version>.tgz` and
+   `liquio-external-reader-igrantio-plugin-<version>.tgz` (both also ship in
+   the hand-over folder).
+3. Rebuild the **cabinet-front** image — it now contains the
+   `igrant.credential` control.
+
+## Step 2 — Wire the plugins into the services
+
+Copy from `config-templates/` into the deployment's config volume and adjust:
+
+1. `config/event/plugins.json` — enable the `igrant` plugin. With tarballs,
+   put them in `config/event/plugins-local/` and use a
+   `file:/var/www/config/plugins-local/<tarball>` spec; with a registry, use
+   `@liquio/event-igrantio-plugin@<version>`. Set
+   `options.settingsRegister = { url: "http://register:8103", token: <register
+   token from requester.json>, registerId: 200, keyId: 200 }`.
+2. `config/event/requester.json` — add
+   `"externalService": { "igrant": { "providerType": "plugin", "pluginName": "igrant" } }`.
+3. `config/external-reader/plugins.json` — same pattern for the reader plugin
+   (name `igrant-reader`, same `settingsRegister`).
+4. `config/external-reader/services.json` — add
+   `"igrant": { "isEnabled": true, "class": "igrant-reader" }`.
+5. Restart `event` and `external-reader`; the `plugin-installer` init step
+   installs the packages at container start. Success shows
+   `plugin-load-success` in both service logs.
+
+## Step 3 — Prepare the iGrant.io organisation (OWS)
+
+You need an **OWS API key** (demo: <https://demo.igrant.io>). For the
+two-organisation story (ministry issues, employer verifies) use two sandbox
+organisations with their own API keys; a single organisation also works.
+
+Create these definitions (dashboard or API; all `trustAnchor: "x509"`):
+
+On the **issuer** organisation (Ministry of Education):
+
+1. Credential definition **Learner Profile** — `dc+sd-jwt`,
+   `vct: LearnerProfile`, revocation on, claims: `ulid, given_name,
+   family_name, birthdate, id_number, phone, email, institution,
+   programme_name`. Give it a display name — a wallet may drop a nameless
+   card.
+2. Credential definition **Educational Institution Certificate** —
+   `vct: EducationalInstitutionCertificate`, revocation on,
+   **`supportInteractiveAuthorisationEndpoint: true`** (mandatory for the
+   pay-inside-the-QR flow), claims: the nine above plus `programme_level,
+   final_outcome, issue_date`.
+3. Presentation definition **Learner PID sign-in** — one DCQL credential,
+   `vct: urn:eu.europa.ec.eudi:pid:1`, claims `given_name, family_name,
+   birthdate, email`.
+4. Presentation definition **Learner profile check** —
+   `vct: LearnerProfile`, claims `ulid, given_name, family_name, birthdate,
+   id_number, phone, email, institution, programme_name`.
+5. Two payment presentation definitions with
+   `transactionDataDefinitionType: "payment"` — one for the TS12 payment
+   **account** credential vct, one for the payment **card** credential vct.
+
+On the **verifier** organisation (employer):
+
+6. Presentation definition **Job application check** — one DCQL query with
+   two credentials: `pid` (claims `given_name, family_name, email`) and
+   `certificate` (`vct: EducationalInstitutionCertificate`, claims
+   `institution, programme_name, programme_level, final_outcome, issue_date,
+   ulid`). `clientIdScheme: x509_hash`.
+
+**Trust list (critical).** With the x509 anchor, the issuer certificate must
+be **granted on the trust list the wallet consults** (NXD: EAA / Pub-EAA for
+issuers, WRPAC for verifiers). If it is not, the wallet downloads the
+credential, fails the trust check, and silently discards it — the exchange
+still shows `credential_acked` on the server. Check with the public lookup:
+`POST https://trustlist.nxd.foundation/trust-list/lookup` with
+`{"x5c": ["<base64 DER leaf>"]}` must answer `"status": "granted"`.
+
+## Step 4 — Configure Liquio through the UI
+
+1. Import `examples/register-200-200.dat` (admin panel → Registers) and fill
+   one record per tenant: `{ "name": "moe-sandbox", "baseUrl":
+   "https://demo-api.igrant.io", "apiKey": "<issuer key>" }` and
+   `{ "name": "civicworks-sandbox", …, "apiKey": "<verifier key>" }`.
+   Records apply within 60 s (settings cache), no restart.
+2. Import the three workflow files (admin panel → workflow import).
+3. Replace the placeholders in the imported templates (event nodes and the
+   `igrant.credential` controls) with your values:
+
+| Placeholder | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `REPLACE_WITH_SETTINGS_NAME` | Issuer tenant record name (e.g. `moe-sandbox`) |
+| `REPLACE_WITH_EMPLOYER_SETTINGS_NAME` | Verifier tenant record name (e.g. `civicworks-sandbox`) |
+| `REPLACE_WITH_PID_PRESENTATION_DEFINITION_ID` | Step 3.3 |
+| `REPLACE_WITH_LEARNER_PROFILE_DEFINITION_ID` | Step 3.1 |
+| `REPLACE_WITH_LEARNER_PROFILE_PRESENTATION_DEFINITION_ID` | Step 3.4 |
+| `REPLACE_WITH_EDU_CERT_DEFINITION_ID` | Step 3.2 |
+| `REPLACE_WITH_ACCOUNT_PAYMENT_PRESENTATION_DEFINITION_ID` | Step 3.5 (account) |
+| `REPLACE_WITH_CARD_PAYMENT_PRESENTATION_DEFINITION_ID` | Step 3.5 (card) |
+| `REPLACE_WITH_JOB_APPLICATION_PRESENTATION_DEFINITION_ID` | Step 3.6 |
+
+The three services then appear as top-level entries in the cabinet's service
+catalog (they carry no category on purpose).
+
+## Step 5 — Test end to end
+
+On a phone with the **iGrant.io Data Wallet**, load a **PID credential** and a
+**TS12 payment credential** (account or card). Then run the journey in order:
+
+1. *Register as a learner* — share the PID (one scan), the enrolment form
+   fills itself, and the Learner Profile credential lands in the wallet.
+2. *Educational certificate* — share the Learner Profile, choose account or
+   card, and one scan both approves the 10.00 EUR fee and delivers the
+   certificate.
+3. *Apply for a job* — choose a role; one scan shares the PID and the
+   certificate with the employer organisation; the application form fills
+   itself and submits.
+
+To show revocation, run the plugin's `revoke` operation (or revoke via the
+OWS API) on the certificate's exchange id and apply for the job again — the
+verification fails and the service ends on the "Application failed" branch.
